{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Six days, etc.</b> The intention here is to warn them not to go out to gather. And the meaning of <b>it shall not be in it</b> is — this act of gathering shall not be in it, for if it refers to the existence of the manna, He already said ״you will not find it in the field״. Therefore when some of the people went out to gather, HaShem said to them ״How long will you refuse to keep My commandments״ etc. — see that they transgressed a prohibition. And where do we find this warning that He said to them? And if His intention was toward the inference heard from His saying ״six days״ alone, this prohibition would not be called a prohibition but rather a positive commandment, by the rule of a prohibition derived from the implication of a positive commandment (Pesachim 41a), and it would not be fitting to say to them concerning it ״you refuse to keep,״ for the language of keeping is said of a prohibition."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:57.016458200Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}